# Riverpod Test Generator

## What This Skill Does
Generates correctly structured tests for each layer of the architecture.
Picks the right tool, pattern, and fake/mock strategy per layer.

## Test File Location
Test files mirror the feature structure exactly:
```
lib/src/features/tasks/data/supabase_task_repository.dart
→ test/features/tasks/data/supabase_task_repository_test.dart

lib/src/features/tasks/presentation/task_create_controller.dart
→ test/features/tasks/presentation/task_create_controller_test.dart
```

## Layer 1 — Repository Tests (Unit)

Use a `FakeRepository` that implements the abstract interface with
in-memory state. Never mock Supabase directly.

```dart
// test/features/tasks/data/fake_task_repository.dart
class FakeTaskRepository implements TaskRepository {
  final _tasks = <Task>[];
  var _shouldThrow = false;

  void setShouldThrow(bool value) => _shouldThrow = value;

  @override
  Future<List<Task>> getTasksForDate(String userId, DateTime date) async {
    if (_shouldThrow) throw AppException.database('Test error');
    return _tasks
        .where((t) => t.userId == userId && t.assignedDate == date)
        .toList();
  }

  @override
  Future<Task> createTask(Task task) async {
    if (_shouldThrow) throw AppException.database('Test error');
    _tasks.add(task);
    return task;
  }

  @override
  Future<CompleteTaskResult> completeTask(
    String taskId,
    String userId,
  ) async {
    final i = _tasks.indexWhere((t) => t.id == taskId);
    if (i == -1) {
      return const CompleteTaskResult.failure(error: 'Not found');
    }
    _tasks[i] = _tasks[i].copyWith(isCompleted: true);
    return CompleteTaskResult.success(points: _tasks[i].points);
  }
}
```

## Layer 2 — Controller Tests (Unit)

Use `ProviderContainer` with repository override. No Flutter widgets needed.

```dart
// test/features/tasks/presentation/task_create_controller_test.dart
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:flutter_riverpod/flutter_riverpod.dart';

void main() {
  late FakeTaskRepository fakeRepo;
  late ProviderContainer container;

  setUp(() {
    fakeRepo = FakeTaskRepository();
    container = ProviderContainer(
      overrides: [
        taskRepositoryProvider.overrideWithValue(fakeRepo),
      ],
    );
  });

  tearDown(() => container.dispose());

  group('TaskCreateController', () {
    test('createTask succeeds and invalidates tasksForDateProvider', () async {
      // Arrange
      final task = Task(
        id: '1',
        userId: 'user-1',
        title: 'Test task',
        assignedDate: DateTime.now(),
        categoryId: 1,
        points: 5,
      );

      final controller = container.read(
        taskCreateControllerProvider.notifier,
      );

      // Act
      await controller.createTask(task);

      // Assert
      expect(
        container.read(taskCreateControllerProvider),
        const AsyncData<void>(null),
      );
      expect(fakeRepo.tasks, contains(task));
    });

    test('createTask exposes error state on failure', () async {
      // Arrange
      fakeRepo.setShouldThrow(true);
      final controller = container.read(
        taskCreateControllerProvider.notifier,
      );

      // Act
      await controller.createTask(fakeTask);

      // Assert
      expect(
        container.read(taskCreateControllerProvider),
        isA<AsyncError>(),
      );
    });
  });
}
```

## Layer 3 — Widget Tests

Use `ProviderScope` with overrides. Never mock providers directly.

```dart
// test/features/tasks/presentation/task_card_test.dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:flutter_riverpod/flutter_riverpod.dart';

void main() {
  testWidgets('TaskCard shows completed checkmark when task is done',
      (tester) async {
    // Arrange
    final completedTask = Task(
      id: '1',
      userId: 'user-1',
      title: 'Buy groceries',
      assignedDate: DateTime.now(),
      categoryId: 1,
      points: 5,
      isCompleted: true,
    );

    // Act
    await tester.pumpWidget(
      ProviderScope(
        overrides: [
          tasksForDateProvider.overrideWith(
            (_) async => [completedTask],
          ),
        ],
        child: const MaterialApp(home: HomeScreen()),
      ),
    );
    await tester.pumpAndSettle();

    // Assert
    expect(find.text('Buy groceries'), findsOneWidget);
    expect(find.byIcon(Icons.check_circle), findsOneWidget);
  });

  testWidgets('TaskCard shows loading skeleton while fetching',
      (tester) async {
    await tester.pumpWidget(
      ProviderScope(
        overrides: [
          tasksForDateProvider.overrideWith(
            (_) async {
              await Future<void>.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 1));
              return [];
            },
          ),
        ],
        child: const MaterialApp(home: HomeScreen()),
      ),
    );

    // Before settling — loading state
    expect(find.byType(TaskListSkeleton), findsOneWidget);
  });
}
```

## Layer 4 — Integration Tests

Test full user flows end to end.

```dart
// test/features/tasks/integration/task_create_flow_test.dart
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:integration_test/integration_test.dart';

void main() {
  IntegrationTestWidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();

  testWidgets('User creates a task and sees it in the list', (tester) async {
    // Arrange: pump the full app
    await tester.pumpWidget(const ProviderScope(child: App()));
    await tester.pumpAndSettle();

    // Act: navigate to create screen
    await tester.tap(find.byIcon(Icons.add));
    await tester.pumpAndSettle();

    // Fill form
    await tester.enterText(find.byKey(const Key('task_title')), 'New task');
    await tester.tap(find.byKey(const Key('category_fitness')));
    await tester.tap(find.byKey(const Key('submit_button')));
    await tester.pumpAndSettle();

    // Assert: back on home, task visible
    expect(find.text('New task'), findsOneWidget);
  });
}
```

## Test Data Helpers

Keep shared test fixtures in `test/helpers/`:

```dart
// test/helpers/task_fixtures.dart
Task makeTask({
  String id = '1',
  String userId = 'user-1',
  String title = 'Test task',
  int points = 5,
  bool isCompleted = false,
}) =>
    Task(
      id: id,
      userId: userId,
      title: title,
      assignedDate: DateTime.now(),
      categoryId: 1,
      points: points,
      isCompleted: isCompleted,
    );
```

## Rules
- Arrange-Act-Assert structure in every test.
- Use `FakeRepository` over `mocktail` wherever the fake is straightforward.
- Never mock Riverpod providers directly — always use `ProviderScope` overrides.
- Always call `container.dispose()` in `tearDown`.
- Always `await tester.pumpAndSettle()` after async actions in widget tests.
- Test both the happy path and the error path for every controller method.
- Keep test fixtures in `test/helpers/` — never inline complex test data.
